commendation. Let's choose Candidate C? Let's evaluate: strengths: correct decisions quickly, 100% reliable, creates positive atmosphere. Concerns: difficulty communicating ideas, egocentric, not willing to further education. For long-distance pilot, reliability and decision quality are crucial, but communication and teamwork also important. Positive atmosphere suggests good crew cooperation, but difficulty communicating may conflict. Egocentric may affect cooperation.\n\nCandidate B: conscientious, handles stress well, good at weather, excellent computer skills, but can be grumpy and uncooperative. So cooperation concerns.\n\nCandidate A: anticipates dangerous situations, sees complex connections, excellent spatial vision, leadership, but sometimes not good at taking criticism, unorganized.\n\nCandidate D: responds to unexpected events adequately, concentrates, solves problems extremely well, takes responsibility seriously, but regarded as arrogant, weak leadership.\n\nWe need to start discussion, maybe propose Candidate C as leading, but note concerns. Provide evidence. Let's do that.\n\nWe must include METADATA_JSON with vote. So vote Candidate C.\n\nProceed."}
